wine-sg (10.0-1137) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Crash dumps the way Windows writes them (9550-9553). MiniDumpWriteDump,
    which crash reporters (Breakpad, .NET's createdump, games' and
    applications' own handlers) use, now writes the thread info list
    (thread times and start addresses), the memory info list (the whole
    address space) and the unloaded module list (a crash in a DLL that was
    already unloaded can be read); makes every callback Windows makes, so a
    reporter can leave threads or modules out, add or remove memory, cancel
    a dump or take its writes itself; puts in the memory the dump type asks
    for (the PEB and TEBs, the command line and environment, private
    read-write memory as .NET heap dumps need, what the stacks point to,
    code sections, module headers and unwind data), never with overlapping
    ranges; and writes MINIDUMP_MISC_INFO_5 (process times, integrity
    level, time zone, build strings, processor state layout) with the VM
    counters and system memory figures Windows adds to every dump.
    vulkan-1's VK_KHR_display entry points answer as the Khronos loader
    does when no driver offers the extension -- no displays -- instead of
    crashing the program that calls them (9554).

