wine-sg (10.0-1115) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 9101 server: the machine's hive file is closed to people too. On
    Windows the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM hive files are SYSTEM's and
    Administrators', and people read HKLM through the registry, key by key
    as each key's descriptor allows. The shared prefix's system.reg was
    0644 in the Wine group: any person could read every HKLM value whatever
    its key allowed. It is now kept 0600 like the people's hives (written
    so, closed when loaded); people read HKLM through the server as before.
    Gate test-hiveprivate (extended), mutant SG_MUTANT_SYSTEM_HIVE_SHARED.
  * 9102 shell32: CSIDL_COMMON_FAVORITES is the caller's own Favorites, as
    on Windows Vista and later (both are FOLDERID_Favorites, a per-user
    folder). Wine read it from HKLM's Common Favorites, which the account
    that built the prefix filled with its own profile's folder: every
    person got the SYSTEM account's Favorites, now closed to them
    (sg-session 0.1.0-281 makes SYSTEM's profile private, as Windows'
    systemprofile is). Gate test-commonfav (64 and 32-bit), mutant
